window.PET_DATA["knowledge/grammar-08-gerunds-infinitives.json"] = {"id":"grammar-08","type":"grammar","title":"Gerunds & Infinitives","objective":"Know which verbs take -ing and which take to + infinitive — a favourite PET testing point.","sections":[{"heading":"Verbs + -ing","body":"These verbs are followed by `-ing`: enjoy, finish, stop, mind, suggest, practise, keep, avoid, feel like.\n`I enjoy reading.` `Have you finished writing?` `She suggested going by train.`\nAfter prepositions, always use `-ing`: `interested in`, `good at`, `thanks for`, `before leaving`.","bodyZh":"enjoy、finish、stop、mind、suggest、practise、keep、avoid、feel like 后接 -ing。介词后也一律用 -ing。","examples":[{"en":"I'm interested in learning about other cultures.","zh":"我对了解其他文化感兴趣。"},{"en":"Do you mind waiting for ten minutes?","zh":"你介意等十分钟吗？"}],"tip":"Preposition + -ing is a gold rule: good at drawing, afraid of flying, instead of complaining."},{"heading":"Verbs + to + infinitive","body":"These verbs are followed by `to + infinitive`: want, hope, decide, plan, learn, offer, promise, would like, need.\n`We decided to stay at home.` `She hopes to become a nurse.` `Would you like to come with us?`","bodyZh":"want、hope、decide、plan、learn、offer、promise、would like、need 后接 to + 动词原形。","examples":[{"en":"I'm learning to cook Italian food.","zh":"我在学做意大利菜。"},{"en":"He promised to help me move house.","zh":"他答应帮我搬家。"}],"tip":"would like / would love + to is the polite form for invitations: Would you like to join us?"},{"heading":"Verbs with both (meaning changes)","body":"`stop doing` = quit the activity: `He stopped smoking.`\n`stop to do` = stop in order to do something else: `He stopped to smoke.` (= he stopped walking in order to smoke)\n`remember/forget doing` = memory of the past · `remember/forget to do` = task/duty.\n`try doing` = experiment · `try to do` = attempt with effort.","bodyZh":"stop doing 停止做某事；stop to do 停下来去做另一件事。remember/forget doing 记得/忘记做过；remember/forget to do 记得/忘记要去做。","examples":[{"en":"Don't forget to lock the door when you leave.","zh":"离开时别忘了锁门。"},{"en":"I remember visiting this castle as a child.","zh":"我记得小时候参观过这座城堡。"}],"tip":"stop to do vs stop doing appears in multiple-choice cloze almost every year. Learn the pair!"}],"commonErrors":[{"wrong":"I enjoy to play football.","right":"I enjoy playing football.","why":"enjoy takes -ing."},{"wrong":"She wants going home.","right":"She wants to go home.","why":"want takes to + infinitive."},{"wrong":"I'm good in maths.","right":"I'm good at maths.","why":"The fixed preposition is at."},{"wrong":"Don't forget locking the door. (meaning: the task)","right":"Don't forget to lock the door.","why":"For duties/tasks use to + infinitive."}],"summary":{"keyPoints":["-ing verbs: enjoy, finish, stop, mind, suggest, practise.","to + infinitive verbs: want, hope, decide, plan, would like.","Prepositions are always followed by -ing.","stop/remember/forget/try change meaning with -ing vs to."],"mustKnow":["enjoy doing","want to do","good at","stopped to do / stopped doing"]},"linkedPractice":["reading"],"reviewItems":[]};
